<main class="shell container-xxl px-3 px-lg-4">
    <section id="future" class="page-intro">
        <div class="section-heading row g-3 align-items-end">
            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <div class="eyebrow">Future Direction</div>
                <h1>Close with what is stable and what is still changing</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5">
                <p class="body-copy">
                    As of April 13, 2026, NASA states that the Landsat Next project is assessing alternate mission architectures
                    to support more affordable ways to maintain Landsat continuity under the FY26 President's Budget Request.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4 resource-grid">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                <article class="resource-card h-100">
                    <h3>What is stable</h3>
                    <p>The need for repeat global land imaging, calibration quality, long-term consistency, and public access remains clear.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                <article class="resource-card h-100">
                    <h3>What is evolving</h3>
                    <p>The exact mission architecture is being reassessed for affordability and continuity.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                <article class="resource-card h-100">
                    <h3>What users can do now</h3>
                    <p>Build workflows around Landsat 8/9, Collection 2, and HLS while the next-generation architecture is refined.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="page-nav">
            <a class="button" href="/briefing/products">Previous: products</a>
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/briefing/resources">Next: resources</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
